"\n\u001b[36m  ●──●──●\u001b[0m\n\u001b[36m  │╲ │ ╱│\u001b[0m       \u001b[1mcode-review-graph\u001b[0m  \u001b[2mv2.4.0\u001b[0m\n\u001b[36m  ●──\u001b[33m◆\u001b[36m──●\u001b[0m\n\u001b[36m  │╱ │ ╲│\u001b[0m       \u001b[2mStructural knowledge graph for\u001b[0m\n\u001b[36m  ●──●──●\u001b[0m       \u001b[2msmarter code reviews\u001b[0m\n\n  \u001b[1mStart:\u001b[0m code-review-graph install && code-review-graph build\n\n  \u001b[1mSet up:\u001b[0m\n    \u001b[32minstall\u001b[0m          Set up the MCP server, hooks and skills for your AI tools\n    \u001b[32minit\u001b[0m             Same as install\n    \u001b[32muninstall\u001b[0m        Remove what install added\n    \u001b[32mdoctor\u001b[0m           Check which copies run, the graph and the hooks\n\n  \u001b[1mBuild the graph:\u001b[0m\n    \u001b[32mbuild\u001b[0m            Parse every file into a new graph\n    \u001b[32mupdate\u001b[0m           Parse only the files that changed\n    \u001b[32mwatch\u001b[0m            Update the graph as files change\n    \u001b[32mstatus\u001b[0m           Show graph counts\n    \u001b[32mpostprocess\u001b[0m      Redo flows, communities and the search index\n    \u001b[32membed\u001b[0m            Add vectors for search by meaning\n    \u001b[32mforget\u001b[0m           Drop files from the graph\n\n  \u001b[1mReview:\u001b[0m\n    \u001b[32mdetect-changes\u001b[0m   Score the risk of your changes (read-only)\n    \u001b[32mimpact\u001b[0m           Show what a change can reach\n    \u001b[32mdead-code\u001b[0m        Find code that nothing calls or tests\n    \u001b[32mrefactor\u001b[0m         Preview a rename, dead code or suggestions\n\n  \u001b[1mExplore:\u001b[0m\n    \u001b[32mquery\u001b[0m            Callers, callees, imports, tests and more\n    \u001b[32msearch\u001b[0m           Find code by name or keyword\n    \u001b[32marchitecture\u001b[0m     Show the main parts of the code\n    \u001b[32mflows\u001b[0m            List execution flows\n    \u001b[32mflow\u001b[0m             Show one execution flow\n    \u001b[32mcommunities\u001b[0m      List groups of related code\n    \u001b[32mcommunity\u001b[0m        Show one group\n    \u001b[32mlarge-functions\u001b[0m  Find very long functions and classes\n    \u001b[32mvisualize\u001b[0m        Draw the graph as an interactive page\n    \u001b[32mwiki\u001b[0m             Write a Markdown wiki from the graph\n    \u001b[32mcontext-history\u001b[0m  Show the saved-context log\n\n  \u001b[1mServe and more:\u001b[0m\n    \u001b[32mserve\u001b[0m            Start the MCP server (stdio, or --http on localhost)\n    \u001b[32mmcp\u001b[0m              Same as serve\n    \u001b[32mdaemon\u001b[0m           Watch many repositories in the background\n    \u001b[32mregister\u001b[0m         Add a repository to the multi-repo list\n    \u001b[32munregister\u001b[0m       Remove a repository from that list\n    \u001b[32mrepos\u001b[0m            Show the listed repositories\n    \u001b[32meval\u001b[0m             Run the benchmarks\n\n  \u001b[2mRun\u001b[0m \u001b[1mcode-review-graph <command> --help\u001b[0m \u001b[2mfor details\u001b[0m\n\n"
